Z||000012||JSocha||08-18-2001||09:38 PM||||<B>Forgive me...I'm bored since my weekend was ruined and I noticed some of the comments</B>  Not that his helps any...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I sent my sister the link from here on Friday and I didn’t know she had the lyrics to the song.  Apparently, a friend of hers had sent it to her months ago but no link to the actual site with the music.  Thanks AkursedX and here I thought I was the only one that gets bored.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So, anyways, she sent me the lyrics.  A very bad copy I might add as some of the words do not even exsist unless they are broken apart into particulates and then redefined or respelled.  If somebody has the actual “good” and/or “original” lyrics, send them to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>The lyrics I posted Friday made no sense once I looked at them in the form they are when I translated them because it is a really hashed version of the lyrics and my sound card in my computer does not work so I am unable to review it again now.  However, since I did have a chance to listen to the song briefly on Friday (thanks again AkursedX), a childrens song for “Good”, this is basically how it translates out below.<P>You have to understand that Japanese songs sound one way but have an underlying meaning.   Some are really bad haiku’s if you ask me.<P>A words “tonal” inflections to an identically spelled word can have two or more meanings based on the way it is said.  Like if I was to say the word “desu” and then say it again only changing the tonal inflections slightly to the point where you would not notice them, unless you have lived and heard the language repeatedly, you would never notice I said and meant the word another way.  Again, I can’t listen to it to translate it better at this time and am going both from the lyrics and what I remember on Friday.<P>Also, some of the words can be formal Names, like the lastname Dobbs.  If used one way it means one thing, but as a last name, it means “Extremly Ugly One”.  I’m also “self-taught” so I never get a chance to hear the language to know if I am pronouncing the words right, but I am sure in a crunch, I can marry a dog to the toilet. Hehehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I miss Japanese TV from Primestar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><FONT SIZE="3"><B><u>One Hundred Fifty One</u></B></FONT><P>A small group of harmonious monks.<BR>In spite of absolute shrewdness<BR>Strive for good!<P>Definitely sum the monks,<BR>Clearly, precisely, in plenty, <BR>Number one hundred fifty one!<P>A small quantity evoke adherent courage, <BR>Properly the remaining group go {geetto=gate}!<P>The feeling nature sets as for encountering altogether<BR>To become as if infactuated<BR>However to carelessly hurt someone’s feelings.<BR>That circle will let me see to forget.<P>Still much more to come<BR>Necessary where easy<BR>A group to cast<P>One hundred fifty one pleasures.<BR>One hundred fifty one dreams.<BR>One hundred fifty one memories.<P>Brilliant Heros! Standing Firm!<P>A small group of harmonious monks.<BR>In spite of absolute shrewdness<BR>Strive for good!<P>Definitely sum the monks,<BR>Clearly, precisely, in plenty, <BR>Number one hundred fifty one!<P>A small quantity evoke adherent courage, <BR>Properly the remaining group go!<P>The feeling nature sets as for encountering altogether<BR>To become as if infactuated<BR>However to carelessly hurt someone’s feelings.<BR>That circle will let me see to forget.<P>Still much more to come<BR>Necessarily where easy<BR>A group to cast<P>One hundred fifty one pleasures.<BR>One hundred fifty one dreams.<BR>One hundred fifty one memories.<P>Brilliant Heros! Standing Firm!<P>The feeling nature sets as for encountering altogether<BR>To become as if infactuated<BR>However to carelessly hurt someone’s feelings.<BR>That circle will let me see to forget.<P>Still much more to come<BR>Necessarily where easy<BR>A circle of friends to cast<P>One hundred fifty one pleasures.<BR>One hundred fifty one dreams.<BR>One hundred fifty one memories.<P>Brilliant Heros! Standing Firm!<P>Well...there you have it.  The Japanese version IMO of "Ring Around the Rosey".<P>I think I am going to head out to Zwarte at the street dance tonight in town and have a few.<P>Later!||||reg||1
